1. Introduction
This Test Plan document outlines the scope, objectives, approach, resources, and schedule for manual testing of the E-Commerce Web Application.

2. Objectives
  - Verify application functionality
  - Identify defects
  - Ensure system stability and usability

3. Scope of Testing
  In Scope:
    - Functional Testing
    - Integration Testing
    - System Testing
    - Regression Testing

  Out of Scope:
    - Automation Testing
    - Performance Testing
    - Security Testing

4. Test Environment
  Operating System: Windows 10
  Browser: Chrome, Firefox
  Testing Type: Manual

5. Test Strategy
  Manual execution of test cases based on requirements. Defects will be logged and tracked until closure.

6. Entry Criteria
  - Application build available
  - Test cases prepared

7. Exit Criteria
  - All critical defects fixed
  - Test cases executed

8. Test Deliverables
  - Test Plan
  - Test Cases
  - Defect Reports
  - Test Summary Report

9. Roles and Responsibilities
  Tester: Execute test cases and report defects
  Developer: Fix reported defects

10. Risks and Mitigation
  Risk: Incomplete requirements
  Mitigation: Clarify with stakeholders

11. Approval
  This test plan is approved and ready for execution.













  
